course: dictionary
lesson: 532
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. Asylum is one of these words. «An asylum seeker has asked for protection and is waiting for an answer» shows that asylum means safety and protection, the help a country gives to people who are in danger.
explain: Look at the other clues in that sentence: seeker, asked, waiting, answer. Someone who asks for asylum is asking another country to let them stay safely. Try the meaning in the sentence: «asked for safety and protection» still makes sense, so you have it right.
explain: Old books and stories can use asylum in a different way, for a large old hospital where people with serious mental illness were once sent. Look for clues such as old, ill, or locked gates. If the sentence is not about safety, check the clues and see whether it is describing an old hospital.
fact: Asylum means safety and protection that a country gives to people who have run away from danger, war or unfair punishment in their own country.
fact: Someone «seeking asylum» is asking another country to let them stay safely. They are called an asylum seeker.
fact: A refugee has fled war or danger. Asylum is the protection a country may give them.
fact: Old-fashioned meaning: an asylum was a large old hospital for people with serious mental illness. This meaning is not used for hospitals today.
fact: Useful phrases: «seek asylum», «claim asylum», «grant asylum», «asylum seeker».
exercise: «An asylum seeker has asked for protection and is waiting for an answer.» What is an asylum seeker? | *A person who is asking another country to let them stay safely | A person who is lost on a walk | A person who runs a large old hospital | A person who builds old castles
exercise: «The old asylum on the hill had locked gates and empty, cold rooms.» What was the asylum in this sentence? | *A large old hospital for people with serious mental illness | A kind of petrol station | A safe country that gives protection | A school for young children
exercise: Which phrase means asking another country for protection? | *Seek asylum | Cross the road | Ride a bike | Count the stars
test: «A refugee has fled war or danger, and asylum is protection given by a country.» What does asylum mean in this sentence? | *Protection given by a country | A petrol station | A large old hospital | A school trip
test: Which meaning of asylum is old-fashioned and not used for hospitals today? | Safety and protection given by a country | A type of boat | *A large old hospital for people with serious mental illness | A group of people who ask questions
exam: Ayo reads «An asylum seeker has asked for protection» and guesses asylum means a sweet shop. What is the best check? | Look up sweet shop in a list of countries | Read the sentence once and move on | *Put sweet shop into the sentence and see if it still makes sense | Choose the longest answer
